{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3f2087c9", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T10:48:00", "text": "@here I've been thinking about our product name, and I believe renaming it from extAIX to ContextForce could better reflect its value to customers. What do you think? I'd love to hear your thoughts and feedback!", "utterranceID": "20261015-0-010af"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261015-0-010af"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_fa16fefb", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T10:49:00", "text": "Sounds good to me. ContextForce is a solid choice and makes a lot of sense for the product.", "utterranceID": "20261015-1-3041a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261015-1-3041a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_82e9fcef", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T10:52:00", "text": "I agree—ContextForce does seem to capture the essence of the product better. It’s a strong move!", "utterranceID": "20261015-2-c95ee"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261015-2-c95ee"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "slack_admin_bot", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T10:53:00", "text": "@eid_3f2087c9 renamed the channel to develop-juliataylor-ContextForce.", "utterranceID": "20261015-18-f730c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261015-18-f730c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_88c661bc", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T20:30:00", "text": "Hi team, I wanted to kick off a discussion about our new customizable dashboard layout feature. I've found some similar features in open-source projects that might give us some inspiration. Let's dive in! 😊", "utterranceID": "20261021-0-9f718"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261021-0-9f718"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_88c661bc", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T20:34:00", "text": "First up, Grafana has a feature called Dynamic Panel Resizing. It allows users to resize panels within their dashboards dynamically, which seems pretty useful for data visualization. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/2707. What do you all think?", "utterranceID": "20261021-1-0370a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261021-1-0370a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_ecaa9084", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T20:37:00", "text": "Hey Emma, that sounds quite similar to what we're aiming for. I like the idea of dynamic resizing; it could really enhance user experience by making dashboards more adaptable to different data sets. Definitely worth considering! 👍", "utterranceID": "20261021-2-5b78f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261021-2-5b78f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8d6fe78d", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T20:42:00", "text": "@eid_88c661bc I agree with Julia. The dynamic resizing could be a game-changer for our users. We should look into how Grafana implemented it and see if we can adapt some of their approaches.", "utterranceID": "20261021-3-e5c03"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261021-3-e5c03"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_88c661bc", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T20:46:00", "text": "Great points, Julia and George! Next, let's look at Kibana's Interactive Widget Arrangement. This feature enables drag-and-drop functionality for widgets on dashboards, allowing users to customize their data views. Check it out here: https://github.com/elastic/kibana/pull/2708.", "utterranceID": "20261021-4-c636c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261021-4-c636c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_14a5889d", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T20:49:00", "text": "Drag-and-drop is a must-have for us, I think. Kibana's approach could give us some good insights into making the interaction smooth and intuitive. @eid_88c661bc, maybe you could explore how they handle widget states during the drag-and-drop process?", "utterranceID": "20261021-5-1ee7f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261021-5-1ee7f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-a13f5d"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_88c661bc", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T20:53:00", "text": "Absolutely, Charlie! I'll dig into Kibana's implementation and see what we can learn from it. Now, onto the last one: Metabase's Customizable Dashboard Grid. It implements a flexible grid system for dashboards, allowing users to rearrange and resize components as needed. Here's the PR: https://github.com/metabase/metabase/pull/2709.", "utterranceID": "20261021-6-659f0"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261021-6-659f0"}

