{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EF_AIX", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-30c6d3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_91523bad", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T14:47:00", "text": "Absolutely, @eid_c9c3d8d5. We should also consider adding a note on recommended hardware specs to ensure consistent performance across devices. 💡", "utterranceID": "20260915-4-9b42e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-4-9b42e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EF_AIX", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-30c6d3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a9002ae2", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T14:48:00", "text": "Regarding integration options, we might want to expand the integration layer section to include potential APIs or connectors. This could help with third-party app compatibility. 🤝", "utterranceID": "20260915-5-b633c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-5-b633c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EF_AIX", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-30c6d3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_1a7d9807", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T14:51:00", "text": "Good point, Bob. We should also address the closed ecosystem approach in the design section. Maybe suggest a more open architecture to enhance flexibility? 🔄", "utterranceID": "20260915-6-0851a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-6-0851a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EF_AIX", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-30c6d3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9db3abf4", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T14:56:00", "text": "For the UI, let's add a subsection on user feedback incorporation. We need to make sure the design is intuitive for non-technical users. Perhaps more user-friendly features or customization options? 🖥️", "utterranceID": "20260915-7-0eb18"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-7-0eb18"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EF_AIX", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-30c6d3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_caa2e58d", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T14:57:00", "text": "And for update disruptions, we should include a section on update management and rollback procedures. Ensuring backward compatibility is crucial for reliability. 🔄", "utterranceID": "20260915-8-d26b9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-8-d26b9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EF_AIX", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-30c6d3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2d8eff4d", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T14:58:00", "text": "Agreed, @eid_caa2e58d. We could also emphasize the importance of thorough testing before deployment in the technical section. 🧪", "utterranceID": "20260915-9-ec3b0"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-9-ec3b0"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EF_AIX", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-30c6d3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a253c65a", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T15:03:00", "text": "Great suggestions, everyone! Here's a quick summary: \n1. Add setup automation tools and detailed user guidance. \n2. Optimize data processing algorithms and specify hardware recommendations. \n3. Expand integration options with APIs/connectors. \n4. Enhance UI with user feedback and customization options. \n5. Improve update management and ensure backward compatibility. \nLet's start drafting these changes and reconvene next week to finalize. Thanks for the input! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260915-10-05054"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-10-05054"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EF_AIX", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-30c6d3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a253c65a", "timestamp": "2026-09-18T04:04:00", "text": "Here is the updated <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/new_ef_aix_technical_specifications_document|Technical Specifications Document>, thank you everyone!", "utterranceID": "20260917-0-57ecd"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260917-0-57ecd"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4b38019b", "timestamp": "2026-10-05T14:17:00", "text": "That's interesting! @eid_bac7c6c4, it seems like their focus is on interoperability, which is quite similar to our goal. We should definitely consider how they handle protocol integration. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20261005-3-6a548"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261005-3-6a548"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2347b567", "timestamp": "2026-10-05T14:18:00", "text": "Agreed, Charlie. Their approach to handling multiple protocols could give us some insights into managing compatibility issues. Maybe we can adapt some of their strategies.", "utterranceID": "20261005-4-6f3d2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261005-4-6f3d2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_bac7c6c4", "timestamp": "2026-10-05T14:23:00", "text": "Great points! I'll take a closer look at their implementation details and see what we can incorporate. Next, we have Apache Kafka's PR 'Support for New Message Formats'. It introduces compatibility with additional message formats to facilitate broader data ingestion capabilities. Check it out here: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/3152", "utterranceID": "20261005-5-cf966"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261005-5-cf966"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4df3bcc2", "timestamp": "2026-10-05T14:27:00", "text": "Kafka's focus on data ingestion is a bit different from our sensor protocols, but their approach to handling diverse data formats could be useful. We might find some valuable patterns there. 📊", "utterranceID": "20261005-6-0445a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261005-6-0445a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4b38019b", "timestamp": "2026-10-05T14:30:00", "text": "True, Alice. Even though it's not directly related, understanding how they manage different formats could help us with data processing in our protocols.", "utterranceID": "20261005-7-1012b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261005-7-1012b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_bac7c6c4", "timestamp": "2026-10-05T14:35:00", "text": "Exactly! I'll see if there are any adaptable ideas from their PR. Lastly, we have TensorFlow's PR 'Expand Model Input Types'. It updates the framework to accept a wider range of input data types, enhancing model flexibility. Here's the link: https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/3153", "utterranceID": "20261005-8-e15b0"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261005-8-e15b0"}
