{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_54905dcb", "timestamp": "2026-10-31T04:24:00", "text": "All criteria are met, approved! Great job, @eid_4df3bcc2! 👏", "utterranceID": "20261030-6-55a93"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261030-6-55a93"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4df3bcc2", "timestamp": "2026-10-31T04:26:00", "text": "Thanks, everyone! Appreciate the quick review and feedback. 😊", "utterranceID": "20261030-7-6927a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261030-7-6927a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3e076e53", "timestamp": "2026-10-31T10:50:00", "text": "Hi team, I wanted to discuss our new PR on JWT token verification. I found some similar features in open-source projects that might give us some insights. Let's dive in! 😊", "utterranceID": "20261031-0-fc977"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261031-0-fc977"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4b38019b", "timestamp": "2026-10-31T10:55:00", "text": "Sounds good, Charlie! What did you find?", "utterranceID": "20261031-1-4f85c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261031-1-4f85c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3e076e53", "timestamp": "2026-10-31T10:56:00", "text": "First up, there's a PR in Express.js that adds middleware for OAuth2 token validation. It focuses on securing API endpoints by validating OAuth2 tokens. You can check it out here: https://github.com/expressjs/express/pull/3169", "utterranceID": "20261031-2-273a6"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261031-2-273a6"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4df3bcc2", "timestamp": "2026-10-31T11:00:00", "text": "OAuth2 is a bit different from JWT, but the concept of securing endpoints is similar. We might be able to borrow some ideas on how they handle token validation. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20261031-3-251fc"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261031-3-251fc"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4b38019b", "timestamp": "2026-10-31T11:02:00", "text": "Yeah, especially how they manage token expiration and error handling. Could be useful for our implementation.", "utterranceID": "20261031-4-09138"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261031-4-09138"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3e076e53", "timestamp": "2026-10-31T11:05:00", "text": "Next, there's a Django PR that implements middleware for CSRF token verification. It's more about securing form submissions, but the approach to middleware might be relevant. Here's the link: https://github.com/django/django/pull/3170", "utterranceID": "20261031-5-881d3"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261031-5-881d3"}

