{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-29b8e9"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_fc0f17c3", "timestamp": "2026-06-24T18:26:00", "text": "Sure thing, Ian! I'll take a closer look at their implementation and see what insights we can gather. Now, let's move on to Apache Superset's [React Component Library for Dashboards](https://github.com/apache/superset/pull/3311). They developed a set of reusable components to streamline dashboard creation. Julia, any thoughts on this?", "utterranceID": "20260624-4-ebbb3"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260624-4-ebbb3"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-29b8e9"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8605f7ee", "timestamp": "2026-06-24T18:27:00", "text": "This is interesting! Superset's approach to creating a library of reusable components could really help us with maintainability and scalability. We should consider how they manage component state and props to ensure reusability. It might be worth exploring their library structure. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260624-5-a5546"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260624-5-a5546"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-29b8e9"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_fc0f17c3", "timestamp": "2026-06-24T18:29:00", "text": "Great point, Julia! Reusability is key for us too. I'll make a note to check out their component library in detail. Lastly, let's look at Grafana's [Dynamic Panel Rendering with React](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/3312). They implemented React components for flexible panel configurations. Charlie, how does this compare to our current setup?", "utterranceID": "20260624-6-29508"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260624-6-29508"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-29b8e9"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0d918f1", "timestamp": "2026-06-24T18:32:00", "text": "Grafana's dynamic panel rendering is quite impressive. Their focus on flexibility and maintainability is something we should aim for. We might want to explore how they handle panel configurations and see if we can incorporate similar flexibility into our components. @eid_fc0f17c3, maybe you can add this to your list too?", "utterranceID": "20260624-7-11caf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260624-7-11caf"}
