{"title": "Fix Inconsistent Timestamp Handling by Standardizing Time Zone Settings", "summary": "This pull request addresses the issue of inconsistent timestamp handling across API flow events. The root cause was identified as a discrepancy in time zone settings across different components of the system, leading to misalignment in event sequences and inaccurate flow analysis. 

To resolve this, the time zone settings have been standardized across all components to ensure consistent timestamp recording. This involved updating configuration files and modifying the timestamp generation logic to use a unified time zone (UTC). 

The fix was tested by running a series of integration tests that simulate API flow events across different components. The tests confirmed that timestamps are now consistently recorded, and event sequences align correctly. Additionally, manual verification was performed to ensure that the changes do not impact other functionalities.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/FlowForce/pull/39", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "True", "number": "39", "state": "closed", "user": {"login": "eid_399e4119"}, "created_at": "2026-10-08T18:08:00", "reviews": [{"state": "APPROVED", "user": {"login": "eid_e5e36dc1"}, "comment": "The changes look good to me. The fix effectively addresses the timestamp inconsistency issue, and the testing confirms that the solution works as intended. Great job on standardizing the time zone settings across the system. Approved!", "submitted_at": "2026-10-08T16:02:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_FlowForce_pull_39"}

