{"Channel": {"name": "develop-hannahmiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f139"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a8a4fdcb", "timestamp": "2026-10-03T20:42:00", "text": "Thanks, Julia! This Kafka feature sounds promising, especially for handling high-throughput scenarios. It could give us some ideas on optimizing our stream processing. We should definitely consider how they manage scalability and performance. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20261003-2-24ec2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261003-2-24ec2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-hannahmiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f139"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_73ca2844", "timestamp": "2026-10-03T20:45:00", "text": "Agreed, David here. Kafka's approach to stream processing is quite robust. We might want to look into their architecture for insights on managing large data volumes efficiently. 👍", "utterranceID": "20261003-3-b0e5e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261003-3-b0e5e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-hannahmiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f139"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8df92d08", "timestamp": "2026-10-03T20:46:00", "text": "Great points! Next, let's check out Apache Flink's Dynamic Data Pipeline Configuration. This feature introduces dynamic configuration for data pipelines to optimize real-time data processing. Here's the link: https://github.com/apache/flink/pull/3632. Thoughts, @eid_73ca2844?", "utterranceID": "20261003-4-f1c54"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261003-4-f1c54"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-hannahmiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f139"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_73ca2844", "timestamp": "2026-10-03T20:47:00", "text": "Dynamic configuration is a game-changer for real-time processing. Flink's approach could help us make our pipelines more flexible and responsive to changes. We should explore how they implement this dynamic aspect. 🔄", "utterranceID": "20261003-5-e5ccb"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261003-5-e5ccb"}

