{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_160fca3c", "timestamp": "2027-04-30T01:14:00", "text": "Will do, @Julia. I'll keep you all posted as I dig into this. Thanks for the support, team! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20270429-6-25f2d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270429-6-25f2d"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7db4431d", "timestamp": "2027-05-01T10:51:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Bottleneck in Data Retrieval' has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/SearchForce/pull/40.", "utterranceID": "20270501-0-b8b9b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270501-0-b8b9b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3fa288cf", "timestamp": "2027-05-01T10:52:00", "text": "Great news, @eid_7db4431d! Can you explain what was causing the bottleneck?", "utterranceID": "20270501-1-84bc6"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270501-1-84bc6"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7db4431d", "timestamp": "2027-05-01T10:57:00", "text": "Sure, Hannah. The root cause was inefficient data retrieval algorithms that were causing excessive I/O operations. This led to increased latency when accessing data from the database.", "utterranceID": "20270501-2-3a594"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270501-2-3a594"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_13786f09", "timestamp": "2027-05-01T10:59:00", "text": "Thanks for the update, David. How did you manage to fix it?", "utterranceID": "20270501-3-04719"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270501-3-04719"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7db4431d", "timestamp": "2027-05-01T11:03:00", "text": "To resolve the issue, I optimized the data retrieval algorithms by implementing a caching mechanism and reducing redundant I/O operations. This significantly improved the data access speed.", "utterranceID": "20270501-4-e7041"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270501-4-e7041"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0b6cb92", "timestamp": "2027-05-01T11:05:00", "text": "Awesome work, David! This should really help improve the performance of SearchForce.", "utterranceID": "20270501-5-3fa41"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270501-5-3fa41"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_160fca3c", "timestamp": "2027-02-16T15:18:00", "text": "I adjusted the Flexbox properties specifically for mobile breakpoints. This involved setting appropriate flex-direction and align-items properties to ensure proper alignment and spacing of UI components on mobile devices.", "utterranceID": "20270216-4-76962"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270216-4-76962"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_990f697c", "timestamp": "2027-02-16T15:23:00", "text": "Awesome work, David! This should improve the user experience significantly on mobile.", "utterranceID": "20270216-5-bdd75"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270216-5-bdd75"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0b6cb92", "timestamp": "2027-02-16T15:24:00", "text": "Agreed, @eid_160fca3c. Thanks for handling this so swiftly!", "utterranceID": "20270216-6-47a68"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270216-6-47a68"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_160fca3c", "timestamp": "2027-02-16T15:28:00", "text": "No problem, happy to help! Let me know if you notice any other issues.", "utterranceID": "20270216-7-b453e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270216-7-b453e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_160fca3c", "timestamp": "2027-02-17T05:18:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug about incorrect entity recognition in ambiguous queries has been resolved. You can check the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/SearchForce/pull/31.", "utterranceID": "20270216-0-e94f5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270216-0-e94f5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_160fca3c", "timestamp": "2027-02-17T05:22:00", "text": "The root cause was that our NLP engine's entity recognition module was having trouble disambiguating terms with multiple meanings based on context. This led to incorrect tagging of entities in search queries.", "utterranceID": "20270216-1-566b1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270216-1-566b1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_160fca3c", "timestamp": "2027-02-17T05:26:00", "text": "To fix this, I implemented a context-aware disambiguation layer that leverages a combination of syntactic and semantic analysis to better understand the context of terms. This should significantly improve the accuracy of entity recognition in ambiguous queries.", "utterranceID": "20270216-2-1e204"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270216-2-1e204"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_990f697c", "timestamp": "2027-02-17T05:30:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_160fca3c! This should really help improve the search results. Thanks for tackling this so quickly.", "utterranceID": "20270216-3-2bd73"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270216-3-2bd73"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0b6cb92", "timestamp": "2027-02-17T05:33:00", "text": "Thanks, David! The context-aware approach sounds like a solid solution. I'll run some tests on my end to verify the improvements.", "utterranceID": "20270216-4-02328"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270216-4-02328"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_160fca3c", "timestamp": "2027-02-17T05:35:00", "text": "Thanks, George and Julia. Let me know if you encounter any issues during testing. I'm here to help!", "utterranceID": "20270216-5-68e36"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270216-5-68e36"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0b6cb92", "timestamp": "2027-02-27T09:54:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug 'Entity Recognition Failure in Ambiguous Queries' has been reopened. It seems like the issue is still affecting CUST-0070. 😕", "utterranceID": "20270227-0-4f9ab"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270227-0-4f9ab"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_160fca3c", "timestamp": "2027-02-27T09:55:00", "text": "@George Davis Oh no, I thought we had this one sorted out! I'll take another look at it. Can you share any new details from the customer?", "utterranceID": "20270227-1-8bac5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270227-1-8bac5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0b6cb92", "timestamp": "2027-02-27T09:56:00", "text": "Sure thing, David. The customer reported that the search results are still not relevant when they use terms like 'Apple' and 'Orange' in the same query. I'll forward you their latest feedback.", "utterranceID": "20270227-2-0e2ef"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270227-2-0e2ef"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-1897c0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_990f697c", "timestamp": "2027-02-27T09:58:00", "text": "Thanks for jumping on this, @David Garcia. Let me know if you need any help with testing or additional data. 👍", "utterranceID": "20270227-3-9e5b7"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270227-3-9e5b7"}

{"Channel": {"name": "planning-shAIX", "channelID": "ch-shaix-1539d5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_aa99608e", "timestamp": "2026-09-24T02:12:00", "text": "Thanks for the input, team! Here's a quick summary: \n- Enhance NLU and training data in 'Intelligent Search Algorithms'\n- Add standardized protocols and error handling in 'Integration'\n- Improve load balancing in 'Scalability'\n- Expand customization in 'User Interface'\n- Strengthen monitoring in 'Performance Monitoring'\nLet's work on these updates and reconvene next week to finalize. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260923-9-0040b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260923-9-0040b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-shAIX", "channelID": "ch-shaix-1539d5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_aa99608e", "timestamp": "2026-09-26T11:47:00", "text": "Here is the updated <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/new_shaix_product_vision_document|Product Vision Document>, thank you everyone!", "utterranceID": "20260926-0-0a300"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260926-0-0a300"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-shAIX", "channelID": "ch-shaix-1539d5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_887367ca", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T17:32:00", "text": "Hi team, let's review the Product Requirements Document and update it based on the latest issues reported. We need to address the AI's misinterpretation of complex queries, integration inconsistencies, slow performance during peak times, customization difficulties, and reliability issues. Let's dive in! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260927-0-496b5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260927-0-496b5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-shAIX", "channelID": "ch-shaix-1539d5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_439a052b", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T17:34:00", "text": "Thanks, George! For the AI misinterpretation issue, I suggest we enhance the 'Intelligent Search Algorithms' section to include improvements in NLU capabilities. We should also consider expanding our training data to cover more complex query patterns. Thoughts, @eid_6d14c4ec?", "utterranceID": "20260927-1-41413"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260927-1-41413"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-shAIX", "channelID": "ch-shaix-1539d5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6d14c4ec", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T17:38:00", "text": "I agree, Alice. We could also add a subsection on 'Context Awareness' to improve how the system handles complex queries. This might involve refining our algorithms to better understand user context. @eid_abff6bea, any UX insights on this?", "utterranceID": "20260927-2-660e2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260927-2-660e2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-shAIX", "channelID": "ch-shaix-1539d5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_abff6bea", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T17:42:00", "text": "Great points, David. From a UX perspective, we should ensure that the interface provides feedback when a query is too complex or misunderstood. This could guide users to rephrase their queries. Adding this to the 'User Interface' section could be beneficial.", "utterranceID": "20260927-3-1ab8e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260927-3-1ab8e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-shAIX", "channelID": "ch-shaix-1539d5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4f731d34", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T17:45:00", "text": "Regarding integration issues, we should update the 'Integration' section to include standardized protocols and improved error handling. This will help with API compatibility and data retrieval consistency. @eid_5a940dab, what do you think?", "utterranceID": "20260927-4-9b87b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260927-4-9b87b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-shAIX", "channelID": "ch-shaix-1539d5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_5a940dab", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T17:47:00", "text": "I agree, Ian. We should also consider adding a monitoring system for third-party integrations to quickly identify and resolve issues. This could be part of the 'Performance Monitoring' section.", "utterranceID": "20260927-5-4a31c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260927-5-4a31c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-shAIX", "channelID": "ch-shaix-1539d5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0b6cb92", "timestamp": "2026-09-27T17:52:00", "text": "For the performance issues during peak times, we should enhance the 'Scalability' section. Let's include strategies for better load balancing and possibly upgrading server resources. @eid_b34186ad, any operational insights?", "utterranceID": "20260927-6-76e76"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260927-6-76e76"}

