{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_ecaa9084", "timestamp": "2026-04-24T18:11:00", "text": "@here check some functionalities of our product here https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/dAIX/demo_1", "utterranceID": "20260424-0-71712"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260424-0-71712"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "slack_admin_bot", "timestamp": "2026-04-26T19:27:00", "text": "@eid_36319f22 joined develop-juliataylor-dAIX.", "utterranceID": "20260426-26-a6ca2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260426-26-a6ca2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_36319f22", "timestamp": "2026-04-27T10:43:00", "text": "@here I've been thinking about our product name, and I believe renaming it from dAIX to TrendForce could better reflect its value to customers. What do you think? I'd love to hear your thoughts and feedback!", "utterranceID": "20260426-0-d9803"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260426-0-d9803"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_fa16fefb", "timestamp": "2026-04-27T10:44:00", "text": "Sounds good to me. TrendForce is a solid choice and makes a lot of sense for the product.", "utterranceID": "20260426-1-583c6"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260426-1-583c6"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_82e9fcef", "timestamp": "2026-04-27T10:49:00", "text": "I agree—TrendForce does seem to capture the essence of the product better. It’s a strong move!", "utterranceID": "20260426-2-b3b17"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260426-2-b3b17"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "slack_admin_bot", "timestamp": "2026-04-27T10:53:00", "text": "@eid_36319f22 renamed the channel to develop-juliataylor-TrendForce.", "utterranceID": "20260427-30-48028"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260427-30-48028"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_0f6b0aea", "timestamp": "2026-05-03T01:47:00", "text": "Hi team, I came across some interesting open-source projects that have implemented features similar to our proposed CRM System Integration. Thought it might be useful to discuss these and see if we can draw any insights. 😊", "utterranceID": "20260502-0-10f2b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260502-0-10f2b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_0f6b0aea", "timestamp": "2026-05-03T01:50:00", "text": "First up, there's a PR from Apache Kafka titled 'GraphQL Schema Registry Integration'. It introduces GraphQL support for their schema registry to enhance data streaming compatibility. Here's the link: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/5104. What do you think, @eid_14a5889d?", "utterranceID": "20260502-1-9728c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260502-1-9728c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_14a5889d", "timestamp": "2026-05-03T01:54:00", "text": "Thanks, Bob! This is interesting. Integrating GraphQL for schema management could streamline our data exchange processes. It seems like a robust approach to ensure compatibility with existing systems. Definitely worth considering for our integration. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260502-2-75809"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260502-2-75809"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_ecaa9084", "timestamp": "2026-05-03T01:56:00", "text": "Agreed, Charlie. The way Kafka handles schema registry with GraphQL could offer us a more flexible data model. We should look into how they manage compatibility with RESTful APIs. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260502-3-07881"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260502-3-07881"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_0f6b0aea", "timestamp": "2026-05-03T01:58:00", "text": "Great points! Next, there's a PR from WordPress called 'GraphQL API for Plugin Data'. It implements a GraphQL API to allow seamless querying of plugin data alongside existing REST endpoints. Check it out here: https://github.com/WordPress/WordPress/pull/5105. Thoughts, Julia?", "utterranceID": "20260502-4-ee238"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260502-4-ee238"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_ecaa9084", "timestamp": "2026-05-03T02:02:00", "text": "This is quite relevant! WordPress's approach to integrating GraphQL with existing REST endpoints could be a good model for us. It might help us maintain backward compatibility while offering new capabilities. We should definitely explore this further. @eid_0f6b0aea, maybe you could dive deeper into this one?", "utterranceID": "20260502-5-555e3"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260502-5-555e3"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch-force-504165"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "slack_admin_bot", "timestamp": "2026-08-02T16:38:00", "text": "@eid_fa16fefb created this channel on 2026-08-02 16:38:00. This is the very beginning of the bug-juliataylor-TrendForce channel.", "utterranceID": "20260802-0-38565"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260802-0-38565"}
