{"title": "Adjust Anomaly Detection Threshold to Reduce False Positives in API Traffic", "summary": "### Summary
The anomaly detection feature in FlowForce was incorrectly flagging normal API traffic patterns as anomalies due to an overly sensitive threshold.

### Changes Made
- Adjusted the anomaly detection threshold to better accommodate expected variations in API traffic.
- Updated the configuration to include a dynamic threshold adjustment based on historical traffic data.

### Testing
- Conducted unit tests to ensure the new threshold settings correctly identify anomalies without flagging normal traffic.
- Performed integration tests with simulated API traffic to validate the effectiveness of the threshold adjustments.
- Reviewed historical traffic data to confirm that the new settings align with expected patterns.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/FlowForce/pull/36", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "True", "number": "36", "state": "closed", "user": {"login": "eid_8605f7ee"}, "created_at": "2026-09-26T23:46:00", "reviews": [{"state": "APPROVED", "user": {"login": "eid_e5e36dc1"}, "comment": "The changes look good to me. The updated threshold settings effectively reduce false positives while maintaining the integrity of anomaly detection. All tests have passed successfully. Approved for merge.", "submitted_at": "2026-09-26T22:01:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_FlowForce_pull_36"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e5e36dc1", "timestamp": "2026-10-06T17:31:00", "text": "Great, Julia! Next, we have a bug in Keycloak titled 'Missing Rate Limiting on Login Endpoint'. The login endpoint lacks sufficient rate limiting, making it vulnerable to brute force attacks. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/keycloak/keycloak/pull/1522. This is quite similar to our 'Insufficient Rate Limiting on Authentication Endpoints'. George, any thoughts?", "utterranceID": "20261006-3-9e0ec"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261006-3-9e0ec"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-10-06T17:33:00", "text": "Absolutely, Alice. This is very similar to what we're dealing with. I'll check out the Keycloak PR to see how they implemented rate limiting and if we can adopt a similar strategy for our Security & Authentication Module. 🔒", "utterranceID": "20261006-4-159c2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261006-4-159c2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e5e36dc1", "timestamp": "2026-10-06T17:36:00", "text": "Awesome, thanks George! Lastly, there's an issue in Kubernetes titled 'Inefficient Pod Scheduling'. Pods are being scheduled through unnecessary nodes, causing increased latency and resource usage. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/1523. Ian, this seems to align with our 'Redundant API Call Routing' problem. What do you think?", "utterranceID": "20261006-5-0aadf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261006-5-0aadf"}
