{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9a7b2132", "timestamp": "2026-10-06T17:55:00", "text": "Agreed, let's optimize those flows! 🔄", "utterranceID": "20261006-10-7dbc9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261006-10-7dbc9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_399e4119", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T22:14:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug about inconsistent timestamp handling has been resolved. You can check the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/FlowForce/pull/39.", "utterranceID": "20261008-0-3bd0a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-0-3bd0a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_399e4119", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T22:16:00", "text": "The root cause was a discrepancy in time zone settings across different components of the system, which led to inconsistent timestamp recording.", "utterranceID": "20261008-1-01f4a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-1-01f4a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_399e4119", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T22:21:00", "text": "To fix this, I standardized the time zone settings across all components to UTC. This ensures that all timestamps are recorded consistently, aligning the sequence of events accurately.", "utterranceID": "20261008-2-c6690"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-2-c6690"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9a7b2132", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T22:22:00", "text": "Great work, Fiona! Thanks for getting this sorted out so quickly. This should really help with our flow analysis accuracy.", "utterranceID": "20261008-3-b7224"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-3-b7224"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T22:25:00", "text": "Thanks, @eid_399e4119! I've been seeing some oddities in the event sequences, so this fix is much appreciated.", "utterranceID": "20261008-4-3445d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261008-4-3445d"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:00:00", "text": "Hi team, I've found some interesting open-source bugs that might help us with our current Salesforce issues. Let's take a look at them together! 😊", "utterranceID": "20261116-0-f682a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-0-f682a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:04:00", "text": "First, we have a bug in Grafana titled 'Incorrect Data Aggregation in Dashboard Panels'. It seems similar to our 'Incorrect Data Aggregation in Summary Views' issue. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/1537. Ian, what do you think? Could this provide some insights for our problem?", "utterranceID": "20261116-1-b2d70"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-1-b2d70"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d098d618", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:07:00", "text": "Thanks, Alice! This Grafana issue does seem quite similar to what we're seeing. I'll review the PR to see how they approached the fix. It might give us some ideas on how to tackle our data aggregation problem. 👍", "utterranceID": "20261116-2-3640c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-2-3640c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:10:00", "text": "Great! Next up is a bug in Kibana titled 'Delayed Data Refresh in Visualizations'. This aligns with our 'Delayed Data Refresh in Real-Time Dashboards' issue. Check out the PR here: https://github.com/elastic/kibana/pull/1538. Charlie, could you take a look and see if there's anything we can learn from their approach?", "utterranceID": "20261116-3-96548"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-3-96548"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0d918f1", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:12:00", "text": "Sure thing, Alice! I'll dive into the Kibana PR and see how they handled the refresh delays. Hopefully, it will shed some light on our dashboard refresh issue. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20261116-4-54e6f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-4-54e6f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:15:00", "text": "Awesome, thanks! Lastly, there's a PostgreSQL bug titled 'Data Loss During High-Volume Transactions'. This is quite similar to our 'Data Loss During High-Volume Transactions' issue. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/postgres/postgres/pull/1539. Ian, since you're already looking into our data loss issue, could you also review this one?", "utterranceID": "20261116-5-d177e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-5-d177e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d098d618", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:19:00", "text": "Absolutely, Alice. I'll check out the PostgreSQL PR and see if their solution can be adapted to our situation. I'll keep everyone posted on what I find. 💪", "utterranceID": "20261116-6-c282b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-6-c282b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:23:00", "text": "Thanks, Ian and Charlie! Let's keep these open-source solutions in mind as we work on our fixes. Feel free to reach out if you need any help or want to discuss further. Let's get these issues resolved! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20261116-7-5df7b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-7-5df7b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0d918f1", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:26:00", "text": "Will do! Thanks for coordinating, Alice. Let's get to work! 🔧", "utterranceID": "20261116-8-5353b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-8-5353b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0d918f1", "timestamp": "2026-11-18T09:51:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Delayed Data Refresh in Real-Time Dashboards' has been resolved. You can check out the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/FlowForce/pull/48.", "utterranceID": "20261118-0-c65a8"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261118-0-c65a8"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0d918f1", "timestamp": "2026-11-18T09:53:00", "text": "The root cause was a bottleneck in the data synchronization process between the API flow optimizer and the visualization module. It wasn't optimized for real-time data streams, which led to the delays.", "utterranceID": "20261118-1-46d0f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261118-1-46d0f"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f2474622", "timestamp": "2026-08-27T13:24:00", "text": "To fix this, I updated the transformation logic to ensure that field mappings are dynamically adjusted based on the latest schema definitions. This should prevent any future mismatches during updates.", "utterranceID": "20260827-2-ed846"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260827-2-ed846"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e5e36dc1", "timestamp": "2026-08-27T13:29:00", "text": "Great work, George! Thanks for resolving this so quickly. I'll review the changes and run some tests on my end.", "utterranceID": "20260827-3-74645"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260827-3-74645"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-08-27T13:33:00", "text": "Thanks, @eid_f2474622. This should help improve the accuracy of our data analysis. Let me know if you need any additional testing from my side.", "utterranceID": "20260827-4-f5d25"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260827-4-f5d25"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f2474622", "timestamp": "2026-08-27T13:36:00", "text": "Thanks, Alice and George. Please let me know if you encounter any issues during testing. I'm here to help!", "utterranceID": "20260827-5-b1162"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260827-5-b1162"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f2474622", "timestamp": "2026-08-29T06:48:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Insecure API Key Storage' has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/FlowForce/pull/32.", "utterranceID": "20260828-0-0d872"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260828-0-0d872"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f2474622", "timestamp": "2026-08-29T06:49:00", "text": "The root cause was the lack of encryption for API keys in the database, which was an oversight in our data storage design.", "utterranceID": "20260828-1-3bdb3"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260828-1-3bdb3"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f2474622", "timestamp": "2026-08-29T06:52:00", "text": "To fix this, I implemented AES-256 encryption for all API keys before storing them in the database. This ensures that even if the database is accessed without authorization, the keys remain secure.", "utterranceID": "20260828-2-f3c68"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260828-2-f3c68"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e5e36dc1", "timestamp": "2026-08-29T06:56:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_f2474622! Encrypting the keys is definitely the right approach. Thanks for handling this so quickly.", "utterranceID": "20260828-3-d68f9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260828-3-d68f9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-08-29T07:00:00", "text": "Thanks, George Martinez. This fix will definitely enhance our security posture. Do we need to rotate the existing keys?", "utterranceID": "20260828-4-61ed3"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260828-4-61ed3"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f2474622", "timestamp": "2026-08-29T07:02:00", "text": "Yes, @eid_71071933, we'll need to rotate the existing keys to ensure they're all encrypted. I'll coordinate with the DevOps team to schedule this.", "utterranceID": "20260828-5-fb2af"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260828-5-fb2af"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e5e36dc1", "timestamp": "2026-08-29T07:07:00", "text": "Sounds good. Let me know if you need any help with the coordination. Thanks again, George!", "utterranceID": "20260828-6-0b795"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260828-6-0b795"}
