{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_5fdedf85", "timestamp": "2026-05-20T22:45:00", "text": "First up, we have a feature from Apache Kafka: Dynamic Topic Configuration Management. This PR implements a flexible schema for managing dynamic configurations of Kafka topics to support evolving data streaming needs. You can check it out here: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/2332", "utterranceID": "20260520-1-f61d5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260520-1-f61d5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8a3b36d4", "timestamp": "2026-05-20T22:46:00", "text": "That sounds interesting! Kafka's approach to dynamic configurations could be really useful for us, especially in terms of flexibility. We might be able to adapt some of their ideas for our schema. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260520-2-86201"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260520-2-86201"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgebrown-ForecastForce", "channelID": "ch-staix-a5ff21"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_dbc6178f", "timestamp": "2026-05-20T22:48:00", "text": "@eid_8a3b36d4 I agree. The way Kafka handles evolving needs could align well with our goal of future-proofing the schema. Let's keep this one in mind!", "utterranceID": "20260520-3-9f398"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260520-3-9f398"}
