{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iansmith-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-aa8bc4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e9652ef0", "timestamp": "2026-11-19T13:13:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug about inconsistent timestamp logging has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/AutoTuneForce/pull/42.", "utterranceID": "20261119-0-504c3"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261119-0-504c3"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iansmith-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-aa8bc4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6f719d21", "timestamp": "2026-11-19T13:16:00", "text": "Great news, @eid_e9652ef0! Can you remind us what was causing the issue?", "utterranceID": "20261119-1-e99cd"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261119-1-e99cd"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-15T23:51:00", "text": "Sure, Ian. I implemented a locking mechanism around the log writing process. This ensures that only one process can write to the log at a time, preventing the race condition and eliminating duplicate entries.", "utterranceID": "20261215-3-c3fac"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261215-3-c3fac"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-15T23:52:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_6a0f49ba! This should help us maintain accurate log data moving forward.", "utterranceID": "20261215-4-6791b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261215-4-6791b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-15T23:55:00", "text": "Thanks, Ian. If anyone encounters any more issues or has questions, feel free to reach out!", "utterranceID": "20261215-5-f794a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261215-5-f794a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-16T14:00:00", "text": "Hi team, the customer has reopened the 'Log Entry Duplication' bug. It seems like the issue is still persisting for some training events. 😕", "utterranceID": "20261216-0-d87d9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261216-0-d87d9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-16T14:04:00", "text": "Oh no, that's unexpected! I thought we had it resolved. 😅 @Ian Taylor, do we have any new details on what might be causing it this time?", "utterranceID": "20261216-1-65eff"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261216-1-65eff"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-16T14:06:00", "text": "Hey George, they mentioned that the duplication is still affecting their audit process, especially with the recent batch of training events. It seems like the fix didn't cover all scenarios. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20261216-2-71e95"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261216-2-71e95"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-16T14:08:00", "text": "Got it, thanks for the update, Ian. I'll take another look at the logging system and see if there's a pattern we're missing. 🔍", "utterranceID": "20261216-3-91475"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261216-3-91475"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-16T14:10:00", "text": "Appreciate it, George! Let's make sure we get this sorted out for CUST-0053. I'll reassign the bug to you in the system. 👍", "utterranceID": "20261216-4-39e63"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261216-4-39e63"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-16T14:13:00", "text": "Sounds good, I'll keep you posted on what I find. Thanks for the heads-up, Ian! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20261216-5-df586"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261216-5-df586"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:01:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug about improper session management in the auto-tuning process has been resolved. You can check the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/AutoTuneForce/pull/47.", "utterranceID": "20261217-0-0a93f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-0-0a93f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:03:00", "text": "Great news, @eid_6a0f49ba! Can you explain what the root cause was?", "utterranceID": "20261217-1-6e78d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-1-6e78d"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:06:00", "text": "Sure, Ian. The root cause was a failure to implement robust session management practices. Specifically, session tokens used during the auto-tuning process weren't being invalidated in a timely manner. This left them vulnerable to hijacking, allowing attackers to alter model parameters.", "utterranceID": "20261217-2-7637c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-2-7637c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:07:00", "text": "Got it. How did you manage to fix it?", "utterranceID": "20261217-3-4d32c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-3-4d32c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:10:00", "text": "We addressed the issue by implementing a more secure session management protocol. Now, session tokens are automatically invalidated after each tuning session. Additionally, we've added checks to ensure tokens are only valid for a single use, reducing the risk of them being reused maliciously.", "utterranceID": "20261217-4-44acb"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-4-44acb"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_961f0487", "timestamp": "2026-12-29T05:37:00", "text": "To fix this, I implemented a more efficient rendering strategy by offloading the graph rendering to a web worker. This keeps the UI thread free and responsive, even with large parameter sets.", "utterranceID": "20261228-2-c272b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261228-2-c272b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8c71a7a9", "timestamp": "2026-12-29T05:39:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_961f0487! Offloading to a web worker sounds like a smart solution.", "utterranceID": "20261228-3-0e40f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261228-3-0e40f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_ea95d983", "timestamp": "2026-12-29T05:44:00", "text": "Thanks, Alice! This should really improve the user experience during those heavy optimization tasks.", "utterranceID": "20261228-4-3b151"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261228-4-3b151"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_961f0487", "timestamp": "2026-12-29T05:46:00", "text": "Thanks, @eid_8c71a7a9 and Emma! Let me know if you encounter any more issues or if there's anything else I can help with.", "utterranceID": "20261228-5-b8539"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261228-5-b8539"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8c71a7a9", "timestamp": "2027-01-10T13:05:00", "text": "Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with AutoTuneForce that we need to address. Let's go through them one by one. 😊", "utterranceID": "20270110-0-c80ff"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270110-0-c80ff"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8c71a7a9", "timestamp": "2027-01-10T13:08:00", "text": "First up, we have an issue titled 'Missing Log Entries for Parameter Adjustments'. The problem is that certain parameter adjustments during model training aren't being logged. This affects the Database Logging System and impacts customer CUST-0116. Users can't accurately audit model training processes, which could lead to compliance issues. @eid_576f3f62, this one's for you.", "utterranceID": "20270110-1-4a0ff"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270110-1-4a0ff"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_576f3f62", "timestamp": "2027-01-10T13:13:00", "text": "Got it! I'll start looking into the logging system to ensure all parameter adjustments are properly recorded. Thanks for the heads-up! 👍", "utterranceID": "20270110-2-e3f00"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270110-2-e3f00"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8c71a7a9", "timestamp": "2027-01-10T13:17:00", "text": "Great, thanks! Next, we have 'Faulty Gradient Descent Convergence'. The gradient descent algorithm isn't converging under certain conditions, affecting the Backend Optimization Engine. This is causing decreased model accuracy for customer CUST-0015. @eid_ea95d983, can you take this one?", "utterranceID": "20270110-3-ccb4a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270110-3-ccb4a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_ea95d983", "timestamp": "2027-01-10T13:20:00", "text": "Sure thing! I'll dive into the optimization engine and see what's causing the convergence issues. Let's get that accuracy back on track! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20270110-4-a9ef6"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270110-4-a9ef6"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8c71a7a9", "timestamp": "2027-01-10T13:25:00", "text": "Awesome, thanks! Lastly, there's a 'Security Vulnerability in Parameter Adjustment Module'. There's a security flaw that allows unauthorized users to manipulate model parameters. This affects the Security Layer of the Parameter Adjustment Module and poses a risk to customer CUST-0048. @eid_961f0487, can you handle this?", "utterranceID": "20270110-5-7fafd"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270110-5-7fafd"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_961f0487", "timestamp": "2027-01-10T13:29:00", "text": "Absolutely, I'll prioritize securing that endpoint to prevent any unauthorized access. Security is key! 🔒", "utterranceID": "20270110-6-17758"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270110-6-17758"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8c71a7a9", "timestamp": "2027-01-10T13:34:00", "text": "Thanks, everyone! Let's keep communication open as you work through these issues. Feel free to reach out if you need any help or additional context. 🙌", "utterranceID": "20270110-7-9416c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270110-7-9416c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-hannahmartinez-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-edd459"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_576f3f62", "timestamp": "2027-01-10T13:37:00", "text": "Will do! I'll update once I have more info on the logging issue. 📝", "utterranceID": "20270110-8-1a479"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270110-8-1a479"}

{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_c3aac633", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T20:48:00", "text": "Hey team! 👋 Let's kick off the discussion for the Product Requirements Document for EinsteinAuto-Tuning. We need to outline the key sections and assign tasks. Thoughts? 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260629-0-7b293"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-0-7b293"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e0273792", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T20:50:00", "text": "Sounds good, Julia! I think we should start with defining the scope and objectives. We need to be clear on what 'real-time data' means in this context. @eid_7017b913, any thoughts from the engineering side?", "utterranceID": "20260629-1-9cc33"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-1-9cc33"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7017b913", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T20:55:00", "text": "Absolutely, Bob. We should specify the types of data streams we'll support and how frequently the models will be updated. Also, we need to consider the computational resources required for real-time tuning. 💻", "utterranceID": "20260629-2-a1ff2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-2-a1ff2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d2f0f99a", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T20:56:00", "text": "@here Explore the Optuna library on GitHub, a powerful tool for hyperparameter optimization. It offers features that align with the goals of EinsteinAuto-Tuning. https://github.com/optuna/optuna", "utterranceID": "20260629-34-09d33"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-34-09d33"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7bd2e61a", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T20:56:28", "text": "@here Discover how real-time data can enhance AI models in this blog post. It provides insights relevant to the real-time optimization features of EinsteinAuto-Tuning. https://towardsdatascience.com/real-time-data-in-ai-models-123456789abc", "utterranceID": "20260629-33-d0364"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-33-d0364"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8b14b999", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T20:58:00", "text": "From a QA perspective, we should include a section on testing strategies. We need to ensure the accuracy improvements are measurable and consistent. 📊", "utterranceID": "20260629-3-657b2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-3-657b2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_dc8bf84e", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T20:59:00", "text": "Agreed, Hannah. We should also think about edge cases and how the system handles unexpected data inputs. @eid_6c9bbe3a, any UX considerations we should include?", "utterranceID": "20260629-4-cdf9a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-4-cdf9a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6c9bbe3a", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T21:00:00", "text": "Yes, definitely! We need to ensure the interface for monitoring and adjusting parameters is intuitive. Users should easily understand the impact of changes. Let's include a section on user feedback mechanisms too. 😊", "utterranceID": "20260629-5-09773"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-5-09773"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_c3aac633", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T21:03:00", "text": "Great points, everyone! Let's break this down: \n1. Scope & Objectives - @eid_e0273792 \n2. Data Streams & Computational Needs - @eid_7017b913 \n3. Testing Strategies - @eid_8b14b999 \n4. Edge Cases - @eid_dc8bf84e \n5. UX & Feedback - @eid_6c9bbe3a \nCan we aim to have drafts ready by next Wednesday? 📅", "utterranceID": "20260629-6-ca51e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-6-ca51e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_5318af37", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T21:06:26", "text": "@here Read about the future of AI model tuning in this article. It discusses innovations that are paving the way for solutions like EinsteinAuto-Tuning. https://www.forbes.com/sites/forbestechcouncil/2023/08/10/the-future-of-ai-model-tuning/", "utterranceID": "20260629-37-c91bf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-37-c91bf"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e0273792", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T21:08:00", "text": "Works for me! I'll start drafting the scope section and share it by Monday for feedback. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260629-7-7252f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-7-7252f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-EinsteinAuto-Tuning", "channelID": "ch-uning-f6ee06"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7017b913", "timestamp": "2026-06-29T21:10:00", "text": "I'll dive into the data streams and computational needs. Should have something by Tuesday. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260629-8-93eea"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260629-8-93eea"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_04a698e5", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T23:15:00", "text": "The root cause was the use of deprecated cryptographic protocols that are susceptible to modern attack techniques. Essentially, the data transmission between the client and the Parameter Adjustment Module was using outdated security measures.", "utterranceID": "20261030-1-7d7d3"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261030-1-7d7d3"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_04a698e5", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T23:20:00", "text": "To resolve this, I updated the system to use the latest TLS 1.3 protocol, which provides enhanced security features and better performance. Additionally, I ensured that all cryptographic libraries are up-to-date to prevent any potential vulnerabilities.", "utterranceID": "20261030-2-5df10"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261030-2-5df10"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_36569bb7", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T23:24:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_04a698e5! Thanks for addressing this so quickly. Is there anything specific we need to test on our end?", "utterranceID": "20261030-3-20cf1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261030-3-20cf1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_04a698e5", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T23:28:00", "text": "Thanks, Julia! It would be great if you could run some tests on the data transmission process to ensure everything is functioning correctly with the new protocols. Let me know if you encounter any issues.", "utterranceID": "20261030-4-f8f1b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261030-4-f8f1b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T23:29:00", "text": "Thanks for the update, George Taylor. I'll also review the changes and see if there are any additional security checks we can implement.", "utterranceID": "20261030-5-78314"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261030-5-78314"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T23:32:00", "text": "Nice work, @eid_04a698e5! It's good to know our data transmission is now more secure. Let me know if you need any help with further testing.", "utterranceID": "20261030-6-e38c5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261030-6-e38c5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_04a698e5", "timestamp": "2026-10-30T23:35:00", "text": "Thanks, Ian and George Jones! I appreciate the support. I'll keep you posted if anything else comes up. For now, let's ensure the new protocols are thoroughly tested.", "utterranceID": "20261030-7-74e38"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261030-7-74e38"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_36569bb7", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T15:29:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Network Latency in Data Fetching' has been resolved. You can check out the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/AutoTuneForce/pull/40.", "utterranceID": "20261101-0-1c26f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261101-0-1c26f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_04a698e5", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T15:31:00", "text": "Great news, @eid_36569bb7! Can you explain what was causing the latency issue?", "utterranceID": "20261101-1-33ed1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261101-1-33ed1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_36569bb7", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T15:33:00", "text": "Sure, George. The root cause was suboptimal network routing and a lack of redundancy in our data fetching paths, which led to increased latency.", "utterranceID": "20261101-2-181db"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261101-2-181db"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T15:36:00", "text": "Thanks for the update, Julia. How did you manage to fix it?", "utterranceID": "20261101-3-72c31"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261101-3-72c31"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_36569bb7", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T15:41:00", "text": "To resolve the issue, I optimized the network routing by implementing a more efficient path selection algorithm. Additionally, I added redundancy to the data fetching paths to ensure that if one path is slow, others can compensate. This significantly reduced the latency.", "utterranceID": "20261101-4-7b72b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261101-4-7b72b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T15:44:00", "text": "Awesome work, Julia! This should really help with the model tuning process.", "utterranceID": "20261101-5-146f5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261101-5-146f5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_36569bb7", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T15:48:00", "text": "Thanks, @eid_6a0f49ba! Let me know if you notice any further issues. I'm here to help.", "utterranceID": "20261101-6-89d5e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261101-6-89d5e"}

