{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f2474622", "timestamp": "2026-06-04T02:44:00", "text": "Hi team, 👋 I've been looking into some open-source projects that have implemented features similar to our proposed PR for real-time processing. Let's discuss how these might inform our approach. First up, Apache Kafka has a PR titled 'Optimize Stream Processing Algorithms' which focuses on enhancing throughput and latency. You can check it out here: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/3304. Thoughts? 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260603-0-f07aa"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260603-0-f07aa"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4e8b2cdc", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T16:20:00", "text": "Good catch, Fiona! I was focused on the new protocols and might have overlooked some backward compatibility aspects. I'll work on that and update the PR. Thanks for pointing it out! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20260726-4-42baf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260726-4-42baf"}
