{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f3dc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_dd1ff0ca", "timestamp": "2026-09-02T21:36:00", "text": "Thanks, everyone! Really appreciate the quick reviews and feedback. Glad to hear everything's in order. 😊", "utterranceID": "20260903-7-729fe"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260903-7-729fe"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f3dc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_38700e5f", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T22:55:00", "text": "Hi team, I wanted to discuss the JWT authentication feature we're planning to implement. I found some interesting PRs from open-source projects that might give us some insights. Let's dive in! 😊", "utterranceID": "20260905-0-5b7df"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260905-0-5b7df"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f3dc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_81582c30", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T22:56:00", "text": "Sounds great, Bob! What do you have for us?", "utterranceID": "20260905-1-c2fe8"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260905-1-c2fe8"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f3dc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_38700e5f", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T23:00:00", "text": "First up, we have a PR from the Django project: [Implement JWT Authentication Middleware](https://github.com/django/django/pull/3616). It introduces middleware for JWT authentication to secure Django REST Framework endpoints. This could be useful for understanding how middleware can be structured for JWT handling.", "utterranceID": "20260905-2-4edf2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260905-2-4edf2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f3dc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e6d2ec9d", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T23:03:00", "text": "The middleware approach is interesting. It could help us keep our authentication logic separate and clean. Plus, Django's implementation might have some best practices we can adopt. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260905-3-b0702"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260905-3-b0702"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f3dc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_022d1fd9", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T23:04:00", "text": "I agree with Emma M. Middleware can be a powerful way to handle cross-cutting concerns like authentication. We should definitely consider this pattern.", "utterranceID": "20260905-4-c7eaf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260905-4-c7eaf"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f3dc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_38700e5f", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T23:05:00", "text": "Next, there's a PR from Express.js: [JWT Authentication for API Routes](https://github.com/expressjs/express/pull/3617). This one adds JWT authentication support to protect API routes from unauthorized access. It's more route-focused compared to Django's middleware approach.", "utterranceID": "20260905-5-629c8"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260905-5-629c8"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f3dc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_81582c30", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T23:10:00", "text": "Express.js's route-focused approach might be more flexible for our needs, especially if we want to apply different authentication rules to different endpoints. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260905-6-6992f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260905-6-6992f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-georgemiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f3dc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e6d2ec9d", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T23:13:00", "text": "True, Alice. It could give us more granular control over which routes require authentication. We should weigh this against the middleware approach.", "utterranceID": "20260905-7-8beea"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260905-7-8beea"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-hannahmiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f139"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71a4de1d", "timestamp": "2026-09-13T01:21:00", "text": "Agreed. We should focus on optimizing what we have rather than adding new layers.", "utterranceID": "20260912-7-edb65"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260912-7-edb65"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-hannahmiller-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-42f139"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_32ff39b2", "timestamp": "2026-09-13T01:22:00", "text": "I think we have a consensus. @eid_a8a4fdcb, could you please revert PR# 6?", "utterranceID": "20260912-8-9693f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260912-8-9693f"}
