{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliagarcia-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-f603c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2e1d6568", "timestamp": "2027-02-22T04:35:00", "text": "Thanks, Julia! This Redis issue is spot on with what we're facing. I'll dive into their PR to see how they tackled it and if we can adopt any of their strategies. 😊", "utterranceID": "20270221-4-387c9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270221-4-387c9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliagarcia-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-f603c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8df92d08", "timestamp": "2027-02-22T04:39:00", "text": "Awesome, Fiona! Lastly, there's an Express.js bug titled 'Sensitive Debug Info in API Responses'. It involves API responses inadvertently including debug information, which is a security risk. This is very similar to our 'Exposed Debug Information in API Responses' issue. Check it out here: https://github.com/expressjs/express/pull/414. Hannah, could you take a look at this one too?", "utterranceID": "20270221-5-59330"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270221-5-59330"}

