{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionadavis-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-7ca0da"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_131494b8", "timestamp": "2026-07-13T20:45:00", "text": "Absolutely, Bob Brown. Always happy to share and discuss. Let's keep these points in mind as we evaluate our own offerings and how we can better meet our clients' needs. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260916-11-02d74"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260916-11-02d74"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionadavis-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-7ca0da"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2594f98a", "timestamp": "2026-07-30T00:41:00", "text": "Hi team, I hope you're all doing well! 😊 I wanted to kick off a discussion about our proposed PR to optimize the WebRTC signaling process. I've found some interesting open-source projects that have implemented similar features. Let's dive in and see what we can learn from them!", "utterranceID": "20260729-0-5d25a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260729-0-5d25a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionadavis-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-7ca0da"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2594f98a", "timestamp": "2026-07-30T00:46:00", "text": "First up, we have a PR from Mozilla Firefox titled 'Optimize HTTP/3 Handshake Process'. This PR focuses on reducing latency during the initial connection setup by enhancing the HTTP/3 handshake. You can check it out here: https://github.com/mozilla/gecko-dev/pull/4885. What do you all think? Could this be relevant to our work?", "utterranceID": "20260729-1-d8b2a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260729-1-d8b2a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionadavis-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-7ca0da"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_69130545", "timestamp": "2026-07-30T00:48:00", "text": "Hey @eid_2594f98a, this is interesting! The HTTP/3 handshake optimization seems quite similar to what we're aiming for with WebRTC. Both involve reducing initial connection latency. We might be able to draw parallels in terms of optimizing message exchanges. Definitely worth a deeper look! 🔍", "utterranceID": "20260729-2-def7f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260729-2-def7f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionadavis-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-7ca0da"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_70223d0a", "timestamp": "2026-07-30T00:52:00", "text": "I agree with George. The principles of reducing handshake latency could be applicable to our SDP and ICE candidate exchanges. Let's see if there are specific techniques we can adapt. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260729-3-7e63f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260729-3-7e63f"}
