{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a7dd9c52", "timestamp": "2026-08-19T10:33:00", "text": "First up, we have a feature from TensorFlow: 'User Feedback Loop for Model Predictions'. It collects user feedback on model predictions to improve future accuracy. Here's the link: https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/4897. What do you think, @eid_8cbee5b3?", "utterranceID": "20260819-1-eb286"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-1-eb286"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8cbee5b3", "timestamp": "2026-08-19T10:35:00", "text": "Thanks, Hannah! This is quite similar to what we're aiming for. The feedback loop concept is crucial for iterative improvement. We should definitely consider how they handle feedback collection and integration. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260819-2-5263c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-2-5263c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_724e1180", "timestamp": "2026-08-19T10:38:00", "text": "Agreed, Fiona. The feedback loop is a solid approach. I wonder if they have any specific metrics or methods for evaluating the feedback's impact on model performance. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260819-3-d6e3b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-3-d6e3b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a7dd9c52", "timestamp": "2026-08-19T10:43:00", "text": "Great points! I'll look into their evaluation methods and see if we can adapt any of their strategies. Next, let's check out VSCode's 'Code Suggestion Correction Tracker'. It tracks and learns from user corrections to code suggestions. Here's the link: https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pull/4898. Thoughts, Julia?", "utterranceID": "20260819-4-52ab4"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-4-52ab4"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_724e1180", "timestamp": "2026-08-19T10:45:00", "text": "This is super relevant! VSCode's approach to learning from corrections could directly inform our system. Their focus on enhancing the suggestion engine aligns well with our goals. We should explore how they manage data privacy and user consent. 🔍", "utterranceID": "20260819-5-2f1cf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-5-2f1cf"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8cbee5b3", "timestamp": "2026-08-19T10:50:00", "text": "Absolutely, Julia. Privacy is key. Also, their correction tracking mechanism might offer some technical insights for our implementation. Let's keep this one on our radar. 📌", "utterranceID": "20260819-6-38dac"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-6-38dac"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8cbee5b3", "timestamp": "2026-09-13T20:48:00", "text": "@here try out our product with this live demo https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/CollaborateForce/demo_6", "utterranceID": "20260913-0-ec9ed"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260913-0-ec9ed"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-09-14T07:31:00", "text": "Hi team, I hope you're all doing well! 😊 I wanted to kick off a discussion about our new PR for implementing resolvers for GraphQL queries and mutations. To guide our implementation, I've found some interesting features from open-source projects that might be relevant. Let's dive in!", "utterranceID": "20260913-0-7bd48"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260913-0-7bd48"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-09-14T07:32:00", "text": "First up, we have a feature from Apollo Server: Schema Stitching Enhancements. This PR improves schema stitching capabilities, allowing seamless integration of multiple GraphQL schemas. You can check it out here: https://github.com/apollographql/apollo-server/pull/4912. What do you think, @eid_8cbee5b3?", "utterranceID": "20260913-1-509fe"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260913-1-509fe"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8cbee5b3", "timestamp": "2026-09-14T07:36:00", "text": "Thanks, Emma! This is pretty cool. Schema stitching could definitely help us if we ever need to integrate multiple schemas. It might be overkill for our current needs, but it's worth keeping in mind for future scalability. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260913-2-27cd5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260913-2-27cd5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_724e1180", "timestamp": "2026-09-14T07:39:00", "text": "Agreed, Fiona. I think the seamless integration aspect is particularly interesting. It could simplify our architecture if we decide to expand our GraphQL services. Let's keep this in our back pocket for now. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260913-3-79c3c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260913-3-79c3c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-09-14T07:40:00", "text": "Great points, both of you! Next, let's look at Hasura's feature: Custom Action Handlers. This PR introduces custom action handlers to extend the GraphQL API with business logic. Here's the link: https://github.com/hasura/graphql-engine/pull/4913. Thoughts, Julia?", "utterranceID": "20260913-4-1b76a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260913-4-1b76a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_724e1180", "timestamp": "2026-09-14T07:45:00", "text": "This one is super relevant! Custom action handlers could give us the flexibility to implement business logic directly within our GraphQL layer. It aligns well with our goal of keeping the API layer robust and dynamic. Definitely worth considering! 💡", "utterranceID": "20260913-5-f2cd8"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260913-5-f2cd8"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8cbee5b3", "timestamp": "2026-09-14T07:50:00", "text": "I agree with Julia. This could streamline our process by reducing the need for additional middleware. Plus, it could make our API more intuitive for developers. Let's explore how we can adapt this idea. @eid_446bc3ee, maybe you could look into this further?", "utterranceID": "20260913-6-037d5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260913-6-037d5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-09-14T07:55:00", "text": "Absolutely, I'll dive deeper into Hasura's implementation and see how we can incorporate similar functionality. Now, onto the last one: Prisma's Advanced Query Optimization. This PR implements advanced query optimization techniques to enhance the performance of complex GraphQL queries. Check it out here: https://github.com/prisma/prisma/pull/4914. Fiona, any thoughts?", "utterranceID": "20260913-7-6194a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260913-7-6194a"}

